#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This example mimics the Car-to-Pedestrian Nearside Bicyclist 50 test from the Euro NCAP Vulnerable Road User (VRU) AEB test
#
#In this test the objective is to avoid hitting the crossing bicyclist target (patially blocked by occlusion vehicles), with use of Autonomous Emergency Braking (AEB) - at speeds from 10-60 km/h
#
#There is a camera sensor mounted on the ego vehicle, and a sensor within the bicyclist moving object which senses the ego vehicle front bumper.
#
#A score is tabulated during the run, using the Euro NCAP VRU AEB points schedule for CBNA 50, located in a Generic Table
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

